  "content": {
    "id": "p69-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "In a quadrilateral $ABCD$, $\\angle A=110^\\circ$, $AB=4\\text{ cm}$, $BC=5\\text{ cm}$, $CD=6\\text{ cm}$ and $AD=3\\text{ cm}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p69-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $\\angle C$. Give your answer correct to one decimal place.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$62.4^\\circ$.\n\nFind $BD$ using the cosine rule, then apply the cosine rule in $\\triangle BCD$.",
          "worked": "Draw diagonal $BD$. In $\\triangle ABD$ and then $\\triangle BCD$,\n$$\\begin{align*}BD^2&=4^2+3^2-2(4)(3)\\cos110^\\circ\\\\BD^2&=25-24\\cos110^\\circ\\\\\\cos C&=\\frac{5^2+6^2-BD^2}{2(5)(6)}\\\\\\cos C&=\\frac{36+24\\cos110^\\circ}{60}\\\\C&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{36+24\\cos110^\\circ}{60}\\right)\\\\C&\\approx62.4^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$. Give your answer correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18.93\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\nAdd the areas of $\\triangle ABD$ and $\\triangle BCD$ using $\\tfrac12ab\\sin C$.",
          "worked": "Use the unrounded value of $C$ from part (a).\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{ABD}&=\\tfrac12(4)(3)\\sin110^\\circ=6\\sin110^\\circ\\\\A_{BCD}&=\\tfrac12(5)(6)\\sin C=15\\sin C\\\\A_{ABCD}&=6\\sin110^\\circ+15\\sin C\\\\A_{ABCD}&\\approx18.93\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
